<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis the Stammerer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">846–879</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Louis II of France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis the Stammerer was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, who made him king of Aquitaine in 867. He succeeded his father as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a> in 877 but reigned only until his death in 879. The weakness of the Carolingian line after his death allowed Boso to be elected king of Provence at Mantaille in 879, the first king from outside the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-the-stammerer.jpg" alt="Louis the Stammerer" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cgb.fr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_sous_Louis_II_dit_le_B%C3%A8gue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
